// Ch10 B05 "What went up" (E, 1.5 min), after the Drowner falls. O06: the snagged lights hang a moment,
// then RISE: three slow vertical spirals past the dead crown into the overcast, turning glimmer_lift gold
// (color rule 1). The first time the player sees motes go up in the game. O07: the party watching.
// Nobody has a word for it. The `reedhollow` cue comes in distant, from ahead.
title: ch10_what_went_up
location: ch10/ossa_fen
---
@letterbox on
@camera O06
@vfx glimmer_lift at=drowner_roots count=12 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 4.0
@camera O07
@wait 1.5
Rhen [surprised]: ...Huh. #line:ch10_up_001
@wait 2.0
Ysolde [cold]: That is not the direction. #line:ch10_up_002 #tn:"She means the direction the dead are supposed to go (down, to the sea), by her faith."
// M4-A2P-112 note 4: Pell says it in O07, then walks on ahead (he left the frame before his line).
Pell [neutral]: It is the direction. #line:ch10_up_003
@mark pell root_walk_exit walk
@music reedhollow fade=4.0
@wait 1.5
@letterbox off
@camera release
===
